# Spaghetti Sauce

{ rating="4" image="spaghetti_sauce.jpg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Saute in Olive Oil

- [ ] 2 [onions]{ ing="onions" }, chopped
- [ ] 0.5-1 [green pepper]{ ing="green-pepper" }, chopped
- [ ] 3 stalks [celery]{ ing="celery" }, chopped
- [ ] 5 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, chopped (2.5 tsp minced)
- [ ] 3 [carrot sticks]{ ing="carrot-sticks" }, peeled and coined

### Brown in Pan

- [ ] 1 lb [lean hamburger meat]{ ing="lean-hamburger-meat" } or ground turkey, _brown in pan_

### Remaining Ingredients

- [ ] 3 lbs [whole peeled tomatoes]{ ing="whole-peeled-tomatoes" } (2-3 cans)
- [ ] 1 large can of [water]{ ing="water" } (using the large whole tomato can)
- [ ] 12 oz [tomato paste]{ ing="tomato-paste" } (2 cans)
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [basil]{ ing="basil" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [Worcestershire sauce]{ ing="worcestershire-sauce" } (they use a lot)
- [ ] 1 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [pepper]{ ing="pepper" }
- [ ] 1/2 Tbsp [Tabasco sauce]{ ing="tabasco-sauce" }
- [ ] 2 [bay leaves]{ ing="bay-leaves" }
- [ ] [Spaghetti]{ ing="spaghetti" }, for plating

## Recipe

1. Chop and sauté the ingredients
1. Use the same pan to brown the [hamburger meat]{ ing="lean-hamburger-meat" } and preheat the oven to 350
1. Combine everything into 1-10 large oven-safe dishes. Using a wooden spoon, squish the [tomatoes]{ ing="whole-peeled-tomatoes" }, then stir everything together
1. Cook uncovered for at least 2 hours at 350 (for 4-5 hours, add additional [water]{ ing="water" })

## Notes

1. Leftovers freeze well. This makes at least 10 portions. Good for groups
